  "notes": "Warm off-white (#f3f2ee) ground with a deep teal-black sidebar and teal accent; red reserved for compliance risk. Queue is grouped by resolution category with colored dots (red/amber/teal) and right-aligned helper text ('Needs your call'). Cards carry rounded grey constraint chips (After 12:30 PM, SLP Tue/Thu, Somali). Calendar day cells use diagonal-hatch gradient for blocked days with the blocking reason written in-cell and full reason in accessible name; workable days get teal outline and 'N open'. Exception switches in the calendar are linked to the 'closest paths' option cards in the red callout and recompute the grid live, with a legal note (34 CFR 300.321(e)). Detail pane variant changes per meeting (amber 'Can't be swapped in place' callout, 'Need an exception?' collapsible, time-slot buttons after picking a day)."
